
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Number Multiplier</title>
</head>
<body>
  <input type="number" id="num" placeholder="Enter a number">
  <input type="number" id="multiplier" placeholder="Enter a multiplier">
  <button id="multiply">Multiply</button>
  <p id="result"></p>

  <script>
    document.getElementById('multiply').addEventListener('click', () => {
      let num = parseFloat(document.getElementById('num').value);
      let multiplier = parseFloat(document.getElementById('multiplier').value);
      let result = num * multiplier;
      document.getElementById('result').innerText = `The result is: ${result}`;
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>

Enter a number and a multiplier, and click the "Multiply" button to see the result! 😊
